  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After standard half-space Stokes solvability/regularity and thin-layer Poincare/trace estimates, the remaining construction couples bulk profiles with rescaled depletion-layer profiles through velocity, normal-divergence and stress matching at every fixed order. The human proof adds a normal-component term at order m+2 plus a global divergence corrector so the truncated composite field is continuous and solenoidal with a controllable interface stress residual. These choices are needed before the energy estimate yields the stated O(epsilon^(m+1)) homogeneous H1 remainder; constants may depend on m and no uniform-in-m bound is asserted.",
